---
title: "Starting style"
description: "--<utility>--starting: the value an element animates in from."
section: Modifiers
sectionOrder: 2
order: 3
---

`--<utility>--starting` is the element's `@starting-style` value. When the element first renders, or leaves `display: none` (a popover opening, `hidden` removed), it starts there and a `--transition` animates it to its usual value. Without a transition nothing visible happens.

```html
<div
  style="
    --opacity--starting: 0;
    --opacity: 1;
    --translate--starting: 0 1rem;
    --translate: 0;
    --transition: opacity 0.3s, translate 0.3s;
  "
>
  …
</div>
```

It outranks every other state, has no `--group-*` form, and works without a base where the utility has a default (`--opacity`, `--scale`, `--translate`, `--rotate`). The formatter writes it first among its utility's lines.
